base_p = 12.00
power_t_i = signed (_power_t_i)   : where signed = '-' if tag == 'S', or signed = '+' if ta == 'B';
if (tag == 'B')
_power_t_i = (p_t_i/base_p) * volume_t_i; // more high more power, lower price, lower power, and the (p_t_i / base_p) is the factor of power buy, postive;
else if ( tag == 'S')
_power_t_i = (base_p/p_t_i) * volume_t_i; // lower price more power, more high less power, and the (base/p_t_i) is the factor of power sale, negtive;
endif

sum(power_t_i) is the finnal power of it.

But, the volume_t_i MUST NOT be the deal volume. Consider the following cases:

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Case 1: t1: "1000  B 12.01", t2: "1000  B 12.02", t3: "1000  B 12.03", t4: "1000  B 12.04", t5: "1000  B 12.05";
        sum_power += (power_t1   + power_t2   + power_t3   + power_t4   + power_t5);
                  += (12.01/12.0 + 12.02/12.0 + 12.03/12.0 + 12.04/12.0 + 12.05/12.0) * 1000;

Case 2: t1: "5000  B 12.05";
        sum_power += (power_t1);
                  += (12.05/12.0)*5000
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE: The result is 12.01/12.02/12.03/12.04/12.05 are eaten by Buying, but it does means different power of Buying.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Case 3: t1: "1000  S 12.00", t2: "1000  S 11.99", t3: "1000  S 11.98", t4: "1000  S 11.97", t5: "1000  S 11.96";
        sum_power += (power_t1   + power_t2    + power_t3   + power_t4   + power_t5);
                  -= (12.0/11.99 + 12.00/11.98 + 12.0/11.97 + 12.0/11.96 + 12.0/11.95) * 1000;
                  
Case 4: t1: "5000  S 11.95";
        sum_power += (power_t1);
                  -= (12.0/11.95)*5000
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE: The result is 11.99/11.98/11.97/11.96/11.95 are eaten by Saling, but it does means different power of Saling.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Case 5: t1: "8000  B 12.05", t2: "1000  S 12.05", t3: "1000  S 12.05", t4: "1000  S 12.05";
        sum_power += (power_t1         - power_t2          - power_t3          - power_t4);
                  += (12.05/12.0)*8000 - (12.0/12.05)*1000 - (12.0/12.05)*1000 - (12.0/12.05)*1000    //commission
                  or
                  += (12.05/12.0)*5000 - (12.0/12.05)*1000 - (12.0/12.05)*1000 - (12.0/12.05)*1000    //deal
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE: Of course commission


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Case 6: t1: "8000  B 12.05", t2: "9000  S 12.05";
        sum_power += (power_t1         - power_t2);
                  += (12.05/12.0)*8000 - (12.0/12.05)*9000;                         //commission
                  or
                  += (12.05/12.0)*5000 - (12.0/12.05)*3000;                         //deal
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE: Of course commission


